\f2\b0  is the Python execution backend for the Jupyter Project, providing the default kernel used by Jupyter Notebook, JupyterLab, and related clients. It implements the messaging protocol that lets the notebook interface send Python code to a live interpreter and receive results, powering interactive computing in Python.\
