4-create the model \
The most library which return most of algorithm in machine learning is \
Sklearn \
\
If u want sample design tree classifier\
1- From sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\'97>>package called sklearn and tree is model and in model contains class  \cf2 DecisionTreeClassifier which include DecisionTreeClassifier \
\
2- create instance from this class\
model=  DecisionTreeClassifier()\
Model.fit(X,y)\'97> train it \
\
5- predication  \'97> for array of new values \
predications=model.predict([.[ 21,1],[20.0]  ])\
predications \'97> to inspect element\
\
\
\
\
5-Measure accuracy of ur model\
Data set split 1-70%-80% for training \
2- 30%-20 for testing \
\
We will compare the predications results with result of testing data set\
\
We should split the data set by \
From sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\
x=music_data.drop(columns=[\'91genre\'92])\
y=music_data[\'91genre\'92]\
X_train,X_test,y_train,y_test=train_test_split(X,y,test_size=0.2)\
Model.fit(X_train,y_train)\
predications=model.predict(X_test)\
\
#now we need to compare the  predication result (X_test) with which expected (y_test)\
\
From sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\
Score- accuracy_score(y_test,predications) // y_test (expected values)- predications?(actual value)\
\
It will print the accuracy between  1 and 0 \
\
If we make the train data is less \'97 >the accuracy score will less \
\
To raise the accuracy of model \'97> make big data for tatin (not duplicated- valid data - no missing - big data)\
\
